  "caption": "Quinn started jiu-jitsu with one rule: never tap. Next morning came a stiff neck, a cranky knee and a bonus sore finger.\n\nMost jiu-jitsu injuries happen during sparring, with knees and shoulders most often affected and necks under plenty of load too. Some knee locks can strain the joint before pain gives a warning.\n\nWhat often helps: tap early (it's a skill, not giving up), build up hard rounds gradually, apply leg locks slowly and tap to the position, and do off-mat strength for neck, hips and grip. Headgear may help protect ears.\n\nGet checked for arm tingling or weakness after a neck hit, a knee that gives way, a swollen ear, or headache after a slam.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
